                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "This fixes 3 separate problems: \n1) that extra slash \n2) Certificates should have been part of OpenBMCManager \n3) OpenBMCManager and OpenBMCManager should always be there since they have properties like Certificates and AuthMethods\n\nYou could make that a bit more clear in the commit msg.."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/schema/oem/openbmc/meson.build",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "redfish-oem-manager-fan-data  doesn't work for OpenBMCManager because we also have Certificates.. \n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/cbc02c2edd3d591fadc9af6f61c14e8edf0b93b0/redfish-core/lib/openbmc/openbmc_managers.hpp#L1516"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/schema/oem/openbmc/meson.build",
                    "line": 4,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "That makes sense.\n\nI did this originally because you shouldn't be breaking because someone else checked in a bug in a schema you don't use.  With that said, this LGTM"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/schema/oem/openbmc/meson.build",
                    "line": 2,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "The Account Service is \n\n\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \"AuthMethods\": {\n\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \"BasicAuth\": true,\n\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \"Cookie\": true,\n\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \"SessionToken\": true,\n\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \"TLS\": false,\n\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \"XToken\": true\n\u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 \u00a0 }\n\nI am good with it always being there."
                }
